  "reason": "PaddleOCR loses exact match in every quality tier (clean -6.9, poor -10.9, photo -13.4 points) and in every router input class (scan -3.8, photo -13.5, pdf -13.6, tiff -7.6), is 1.8x slower per page (p50 6.5 s vs 3.6 s) and has lower PHI precision (0.714 vs 0.775). Its PHI recall is higher (0.937 vs 0.889) and its photo CER lower, but no input class gains on the primary metric, so nothing is adopted. Main failure seen: PP-OCRv4 drops the space after label punctuation ('Accession No.ACC-11144883'), which the Tesseract-tuned OCR-first label parser keeps in the value."
